[h1]Questions[/h1]
Ask anything about Cultured Start Reloaded here: how a route or scenario works, whether something is possible, compatibility with another mod, install trouble that is not a bug. One question per reply keeps answers easy to find. Bugs go in the Bug Reports thread, ideas in the Suggestions thread.

[h2]Already answered[/h2]
[list]
    [*][b]What are the three routes?[/b] Vanilla Start (the game exactly as it ships), Cultured Start (a guided narrative through your character's life), and the Start Editor (full manual control over attributes, gear, family, companions, and more).
    [*][b]What are the eight starting scenarios?[/b] Commoner, Mercenary, Landless Vassal, Landed Vassal, Monarch, Outlaw, Caravan Master, and Rebel Clan. Each has its own chapters, starting resources, and consequences.
    [*][b]How do I choose which one I start as?[/b] On Cultured Start you do not choose it: the thirteen scenes decide it, and a screen after them reads your life back and names what you begin as before anything is applied. The Start Editor sets it directly, on the Path and Realm tab.
    [*][b]Can I turn off a start type I don't want?[/b] Yes, in MCM, individually. Turning every one off brings them all back, since a start has to exist. If a life on Cultured Start earns one you have switched off, the screen after the scenes says so and names the nearest one still open.
    [*][b]Does this affect a save already in progress?[/b] No. The mod only runs during character creation on a new campaign.
    [*][b]Does it work with Story Mode?[/b] Yes. You also choose how far along the main story your character already is, and the campaign picks up from there.
    [*][b]Do I need War Sails?[/b] No, and nothing here is disabled without it. If you own it, one scene becomes a hiring waterfront, a life spent at sea comes out with the naval skills for it, and three beginnings at sea open up: a raider in shallow-draft hulls, an admiral seated on a castle with its own port, or a venturer sailing with their own people's caravan. Its items are offered in the gear pickers like the base game's, and its three naval skills are editable in the Start Editor. Without the DLC that chapter is simply not there and the story is unchanged.
    [*][b]What does the Start Editor let me set?[/b] Attributes, skill focus and levels, perks and traits, every gear slot (with culture/class/tier filters or an automatic quartermaster), battle/civilian/stealth outfits, mount, banner, gold, influence, troops, renown, family and companions. It also sets by hand every figure the guided route works out for you: the automatic purse, influence and muster, the provisions plan, how your gear is borne, and the ships under you. Presets save a whole setup, your character and clan names included. It is transactional: closing without saving restores exactly what you had when you opened it.
    [*][b]Will overhaul mods that change gold/tier/troop caps break this?[/b] No. Every bound is read live from the running game, so this mod rescales with those caps instead of breaking.
[/list]

[h2]When asking[/h2]
Say which Bannerlord version you run and which start type or route the question concerns.
